docs {
  Fetches a single BillXpress card and attempts to refresh current details from
  Maplerad.

  The backend always returns the saved BillXpress card when it exists. If the
  Maplerad detail lookup fails, `details` will be `null` and `providerError`
  will explain the provider-side issue.

  Treat PAN, CVV and other sensitive card credentials as sensitive. Never log
  or persist full card credentials on the frontend.

  ## Expected Response

  ```json
  {
    "card": {
      "id": "...",
      "brand": "VISA",
      "currency": "USD",
      "type": "VIRTUAL",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "name": "BillXpress Card",
      "maskedPan": "**** **** **** 1234",
      "balance": 0,
      "maintenanceStatus": "CURRENT"
    },
    "details": {
      "id": "...",
      "status": "ACTIVE"
    },
    "providerError": null
  }
  ```

  ## Provider Detail Failure

  ```json
  {
    "card": {
      "id": "...",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "maskedPan": "**** **** **** 1234"
    },
    "details": null,
    "providerError": {
      "message": "Maplerad request failed",
      "statusCode": 502
    }
  }
  ```

  Frontend should still show the saved `card` object in this case and can show a
  gentle "details temporarily unavailable" state for provider-only data.
}
